# Backend Conventions

## Structure

- `server.js` — Express setup, CORS, route registration
- `routes/` — `auth`, `todos`, `tags`, `data`, `ai` (one file per domain)
- `utils/storage.js` — `readData()`, `writeData()`, `DATA_FILE`
- `middleware/apiAuth.js` — optional `API_KEY` protection for integrations (n8n)

## API Endpoints

| Route | Methods |
|-------|---------|
| `/api/auth/login` | POST |
| `/api/todos`, `/api/todos/:id` | GET, POST / PUT, DELETE |
| `/api/todos/order` | GET, PUT |
| `/api/tags`, `/api/tags/:id` | GET, POST / PUT, DELETE |
| `/api/data/export`, `/api/data/import` | GET, POST |
| `/api/ai/improve-text` | POST |

## Patterns

```javascript
import { readData, writeData } from '../utils/storage.js'
const data = await readData()
// mutate data
await writeData(data)
```

- Generate IDs with `Date.now()`
- Persist entire JSON atomically via `writeData`
- Production: set `DATA_FILE_PATH` for persistent volume
